    <!-- The in-app guide. -->
    <string name="guide_action">Guide</string>
    <string name="guide_title">Getting started</string>
    <string name="guide_connecting">Connecting</string>
    <string name="guide_connecting_body">Plug the synth into the phone’s USB-C port (an OTG adapter, or a USB-C to USB-B cable) and switch it on.\nAllow access once: Oscyl connects and reads every program.\nTap the synth button, top right, for its jobs. No synth? Tap Add a synth there and try one.</string>
    <string name="guide_offline">Working offline</string>
    <string name="guide_offline_body">Import your synth’s library files in Library.\nEdit them anywhere: what Oscyl does not edit stays exactly as it was, so the files stay compatible.</string>
    <string name="guide_editing">Editing</string>
    <string name="guide_editing_body">Open a program from Library and scroll through its stages, or tap one on the strip at the side (slide along it to see their names).\nDrag a knob up or down to turn it; move slowly to turn it finely.\nTap “↶ was” under a control, or double-tap a knob, to put it back. An orange dot marks what you changed.\nTap a picture to open it full screen and drag its handles.</string>
    <string name="guide_auditioning">Auditioning</string>
    <string name="guide_auditioning_body">Turn on Live in the synth button’s sheet: every change plays on the synth at once.\nHold Compare, under the stages, to hear the saved sound; slide to blend it with your edit.\nIn Library, swipe a program to the left to hear it without opening it.</string>
    <string name="guide_generating">Generating sounds</string>
    <string name="guide_generating_body">Pick a character, shape it with the four dials and press Generate for six sounds.\nTap one to hear it, then Keep it: over the program open (an edit you can undo) or in a library.\nVary deals six more like it; Breed with crosses two; the arrows go back to earlier sets.</string>
    <string name="guide_syncing">Syncing</string>
    <string name="guide_syncing_body">Tap Sync on the island to see exactly which slots will change.\nOscyl backs up what they hold, writes only those and checks each one.\nYour edits are never lost: unsynced ones stay, even if the synth is unplugged or the app closes.</string>
    <string name="guide_units">Managing units</string>
    <string name="guide_units_body">Synths of the logue family have slots for user oscillators and effects.\nTap the synth button, then User units: load a unit file into an empty slot, or clear one (a backup is taken first).</string>
    <string name="units_clear_title">Clear “%1$s”?</string>
    <string name="units_clear_body">The slot is emptied on the synth. Oscyl saves a backup of the unit first: Put back, in Backups, loads it again.</string>
    <string name="units_clear_confirm">Clear slot</string>
    <string name="backups_put_back">Put back</string>
